  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IOM Flash Appeal for Ukraine and Neighboring Countries (Health, MHPSS, WASH, PSEA, and CBI initiatives)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The war in Ukraine has triggered one of the largest humanitarian crises on record with over 8 million people displaced in the country and another 5.7 million refugees and 224,000 third country nationals (TCNs) fleeing across borders since the start of the crisis. As the crisis continues to evolve, displacement patterns continue to change. Flexibility to support previously trapped populations in newly accessible areas, and to address new and secondary displacements and returning populations with humanitarian assistance, remains at the forefront of the response. In coordination with the Government of Ukraine and local partners, IOM is increasing access to health, mental health and psychosocial support, and water, sanitation and hygiene (WASH) services for internally displaced persons, host communities, and TCNs in Ukraine in a manner that upholds their rights, dignity and well-being and that is better protected from sexual exploitation and abuse. The aim of the project is to address short term needs and mitigate potential long-term negative psychological effects among conflict-affected populations.</narrative>
  </description>
